Setting up adguard on Ubuntu server 22.04.5 LTS with docker compose 

Firstly you must have docker and docker compose installed

if not you can not follow this link "How to install docker and docker compose"

sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get upgrade -y      # update & upgrade ubuntu server 

after that make a folder inside your ubuntu server 

mkdir -p ~/adguard      # make directory

cd ~/adguard       # change directory 

touch docker-compose.yml       # create file 

after setting yaml file 

docker compose up -d   # to start docker file and make sure you are in the directory that you have docker file 


To access the URL of adguard visit (http://<your_server_ip>:3000)

Optional if you want to use custom ports 

edit your docker file and add this port below 

ports:
  - "53:53/tcp"
  - "53:53/udp"
  - "80:80/tcp"
  - "3000:3000/tcp"        # if any app is running on port 3000 change the left number to 3002 


Remove network_mode: host 

add the above ports 

To access the URL of adguard visit (http://<your_server_ip>:3000)


if you encounter any problem mostly will be with the networking involving ports 

Google,Youtube and ChatGPT is your best friend to solve it 

